{"title":"Career roadmap · Costume Designer","role":"Costume Designer","summary":"A Costume Designer develops clothing and visual costume concepts for film, television, theatre, OTT, advertising, music videos, dance, live performances, fashion productions, and other visual media. The role combines fashion design with character development, storytelling, historical/cultural research, textiles, garment construction, styling, colour, continuity, and production management.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career alignment"},{"type":"p","text":"A Costume Designer develops clothing and visual costume concepts for film, television, theatre, OTT, advertising, music videos, dance, live performances, fashion productions, and other visual media. The role combines fashion design with character development, storytelling, historical/cultural research, textiles, garment construction, styling, colour, continuity, and production management."},{"type":"p","text":"A B.Des in Fashion Design provides a strong foundation, but a successful Costume Designer also needs to understand script interpretation, character psychology, period/cultural costume, sourcing, fittings, budgeting, continuity, and collaboration with directors, actors, stylists, production designers, and costume teams."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical Roles"],"rows":[[{"text":"Entry"},{"text":"Costume Design Intern, Costume Assistant, Wardrobe Assistant"}],[{"text":"Early Career"},{"text":"Assistant Costume Designer, Junior Costume Designer"}],[{"text":"Mid Career"},{"text":"Costume Designer, Costume Supervisor"}],[{"text":"Advanced"},{"text":"Senior Costume Designer, Costume Department Head"}],[{"text":"Leadership"},{"text":"Costume Design Director / Creative Head"}],[{"text":"Independent"},{"text":"Freelance Costume Designer / Costume Studio Founder"}]]}]},{"he